nts) would require all melds to be pungs/kongs, but I have three chows already exposed, so not possible.\n\n\"Full Flush\" (24) requires all one suit, impossible.\n\n\"Mixed Straight\" (8) is possible: three chows of 123, 456, 789 in different suits. I have W2-W3-W4 (234), T3-T4-T5 (345), B7-B8-B9 (789). Not exactly 123, 456, 789. But if I can get a chow of 123 in one suit, 456 in another, 789 in third, that would be Mixed Straight. Currently, I have 234 in Characters, 345 in Bamboo, 789 in Dots. So I am close but not exactly. If I can change my Characters chow to 123 (W1-W2-W3) but I have W2-W3-W4 exposed, cannot change. So Mixed Straight is not possible with exposed melds.\n\n\"Reversible Tiles\" (8) requires specific tiles; my hand doesn't have many.\n\nSo likely my hand will be low scoring. However, I must still try to win. Maybe I can aim for \"Chicken Hand\" (8 points) which is a hand worth 0 fans but with flower tiles? Actually Chicken Hand is worth 8 points explicitly, but it requires the hand to have no other scoring patterns except possibly flowers. But in Chinese Standard, Chicken Hand is a pattern worth 8 points, meaning if I have a hand that would otherwise score 0, I get 8 points. So if I can form a winning hand that has no other patterns (like no honors, no terminals, no chow/pung patterns), I could get 8 via Chicken Hand. But \"All Chows\" gives 2, so that would disqualify Chicken Hand because it has a pattern. So if I have \"All Chows\", I cannot have Chicken Hand. So I need to avoid \"All Chows\" to get Chicken Hand? But \"All Chows\" is only if all four melds are chows. If I make my fourth meld a pung instead of a chow, then I won't have \"All Chows\". Then my hand might have no patterns except maybe \"No Honors\" (1) or \"All Simples\" (2) if no terminals. But I have B9 terminal, so \"All Simples\" not possible. So if I win with a pung and three chows, I might have only \"No Honors\" (1) and maybe \"Pung of Terminals or Honors\" if the pung is of